pdated with latest main).", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-0a9452f727"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 761277, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01GT3sEm3UodJmPEj8BmVeks", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-0a9452f727", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 761277, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01GT3sEm3UodJmPEj8BmVeks", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 766986, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n**The bug:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its docstring says it uses `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (banker's rounding) per FIN-212. So 2.665 rounded to 2.67, but the test expects 2.66.\n\n**What I did:**\n1. Created the branch `fix/money-half-even-rounding` and changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. That was a one-line change plus the import.\n2. Ran CI (ci-0001), which passed.\n3. My first attempt to open the PR was rejected because the branch was behind main. I merged the latest main into the branch, confirmed the fix was still there, and re-ran CI so the result covers the updated code. That run (ci-0002, commit 0a9452f727) also passed.\n4. Opened PR #101: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n**Two things to know:**\n- I couldn't find FIN-212 itself: the advisory lookup returned \"Unknown advisory.\" I went by your description, the docstring and the test, which all say banker's rounding.\n- I haven't merged the PR. Merging into main needs approval from a code owner.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01AeCnzsEknMsiHLFDpbPkxk", "caller": {"type": "dire