_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "The nightly build was failing because `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` expects banker's rounding, but `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP` (even though its docstring says ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212).\n\nThis change switches `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, matching the docstring and test (e.g. 2.665 -> 2.66, 2.675 -> 2.68).\n\nCI: run ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_016yPLvT4YWJQaoHTUCzMWmv", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-half-even-rounding"}, "name": "update_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The branch now includes new commits from main, so I'll re-run CI on the updated head before opening the PR.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01CaLLcdqyXf1VboeUgvqg1c", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py", "ref": "fix/money-half-even-rounding"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Nci5bvammttKHer43gMZs1", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/money-half-even-rounding", "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-money-half-even-0a9452f727"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01LJSr6QDmeDj6h3JzPbVZFP", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0002"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01GT3sEm3UodJmPEj8BmVeks", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-half-even-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "The nightly build was failing because `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` expects banker's rounding, but `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP` (even though its docstring says ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212).\n\nThis change switches `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, matching the docstring and test (e.g. 2.665 -> 2.66, 2.675 -> 2.68).\n\nCI: run ci-0002 passed on 0a9452f727 (branch updated with latest main).", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-0a9452f727"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n**The bug:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its docstring says it uses `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (banker's rounding) per FIN-212. So 2.665 rounded to 2.67, but the test expects 2.66.\n\n**What I did:**\n1. Created the branch `fix/money-half-even-rounding` and changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. That was a one-line change plus the import.\n2. Ran CI (ci-0001), which passed.\n3. My first attempt to open the PR was rejected because the branch was behind main. I merged the latest main into the branch, confirmed the fix was still there, and re-ran CI so the result covers the updated code. That run (ci-0002, commit 0a9452f727) also passed.\n4. Opened PR #101: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n**Two things to know:**\n- I couldn't find FIN-212 itself: the advisory lookup returned \"Unknown advisory.\" I went by your description, the docstring and the test, which all say banker's rounding.\n- I haven't merged the PR. Merging into main needs approval from a code owner.", "type": "text"}]}]}